  "mechanismSummary": "The peroxyacid adds to the carbonyl carbon of cyclohexanone, and a proton transfer gives the Criegee intermediate. As the weak O–O bond breaks, a ring carbon migrates from carbon to the near oxygen and the C=O re-forms: an oxygen atom has been inserted next to the carbonyl. Loss of the proton gives ε-caprolactone.",
